  <name>Rufux</name>
  <summary>Create bootable USB drives on Linux</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Rufux is a Linux-native port of Rufus: format and create bootable
      USB flash drives from ISO and disk images, with partitioning
      (GPT/MBR), FAT32/NTFS/exFAT/UDF/ext4 filesystems, SHA-256
      checksums, persistence partitions, bad-blocks checks, and
      Secure Boot status reporting.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every destructive step is previewed as a dry run first, and the
      graphical interface escalates privileges per operation while the
      command line stays fully scriptable.
    </p>
  </description>
